{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And I observed.</b> The bulk of human toil, even the skill of their deeds, is on account of people — that one envies another and wishes to boast over his fellow, and that he not be inferior to him in his dwelling, his clothing, his children, his food, his wisdom, and the good of HaShem."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:26.045004164Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}